{
  "version": 1,
  "_rules": [
    "Activity = what the customer thinks they are booking. A tier points at exactly one activity or style via taxonomy_key.",
    "Style = a physically different configuration a customer would filter for AND one venue could offer side by side. Key form: '<activity>.<style>'.",
    "Attribute = a detail of the thing (size, count, model). Never creates a new node.",
    "Games played (8-ball, 9-ball, FIFA, Valorant) are information only, never a node and never a filter.",
    "The owner's tier (name + price) is the package. The taxonomy only classifies it, so PC Gaming has no styles.",
    "Every enum/multi attribute implicitly allows 'Don't know' (stored as null). Optional attributes never filter a listing out.",
    "bookable_now = our hourly unit booking already fits it. false = discovery listing only.",
    "billing_unit is display information only; pricing stays per hour per seat."
  ],
